From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] emacs: Leave the replied tag to notmuch new
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rtxlxuxxwppxumuqnrszqlsumvrzvouo

notmuch-emacs tags the message being answered +replied from
message-send-hook, before the send happens, so a reply that fails to
send still marks the original replied. The tag carries no information
of its own: the post-new hook recomputes replied from the In-Reply-To
headers on the list, and resets it on every notmuch new. Tagging early
only shows a state the list does not have yet, and may never have.
---
change-id: rtxlxuxxwppxumuqnrszqlsumvrzvouo

 dotfiles/emacs/init.el | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dotfiles/emacs/init.el b/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
index e620223..9fc0f0c 100644
--- a/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
+++ b/dotfiles/emacs/init.el
@@ -576,6 +576,8 @@ and prefixes every line with \"> \"."
 (setq sendmail-program
       (expand-file-name "libexec/maildir-deliver.sh" user-emacs-directory))
 (setq notmuch-draft-tags '("+draft"))
+;; notmuch new derives replied from the list; don't tag before sending.
+(setq notmuch-message-replied-tags nil)
 (setq notmuch-search-oldest-first nil)
 (setq notmuch-show-only-matching-messages t)
 (setq notmuch-show-mark-read-tags nil)

